glen ,
in case you have not seen this pg & e motion . pg & e is calling it quits on its
backbone open season application . it is clear that pg & e can not maintain
its plan roll out for this open season and therefore one of the primary
reasons to do this at all ( keeping pace with ruby and sonoran pipelines ) has
been made impossible . next , there was a growing consensus that market
participants required more information concerning backbone rates and
operational structure . these items would be included in the long awaited gas
accord ii filing . pg & e has to file its gas accord ii , then i would expect a
likely re application of an open season . no definite word on when the g ii
will be filed . mark , igs .
